        "original_id": "4d93a3df-6916-5315-b7a8-7aefd78093fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Kuvasz, Bouvier des Ardennes, Maremma Sheepdog, Pyrenean Mountain Dog, Tatra, Cuvac, Šarplaninac, Akbash Dog\n- Places: Hungary, Belgium, Poland, Slovakia, Turkey\n- Concepts: dog breeds, livestock dogs, shared ancestry, similar breeds\n\nFacts:\n- The Kuvasz is an ancient breed of livestock dog of Hungarian origin.\n- The Bouvier des Ardennes is a rare dog breed from Belgium.\n- The Maremma Sheepdog is described as similar to the Pyrenean Mountain Dog, the Kuvasz of Hungary, the Tatra of Poland, the Cuvac of Slovakia, and the Šarplaninac.\n- The Maremma Sheepdog and those similar breeds may share a common ancestor.\n- The Akbash Dog of Turkey is also listed as a similar breed to the Maremma Sheepdog.",
